Comment (internal/api/handler/evidence_batch.go:231):
**[Must-fix] Humans troubleshooting automation can't read its batches**

Reviewer decision: batches are submitted by automation, but the person troubleshooting them is usually a human (an admin), and today anyone but the submitter gets 404 with no way around it. The submitter-only rule has no strong reason behind it: the stored evidence is already readable through the evidence read routes. Add a dedicated authz verb that lets its holders read any submitter's batch, admin-only by default.

**Why:** Operators need to troubleshoot automation's batches; submitter-only reads block them without protecting anything the evidence routes don't already expose.
**Fix:** Add evidence:inspect (pdp.go constant + manifest.yaml), grant it to admins only under builtin (users through the admin check, agents/anonymous denied; Cedar admin gets it via "*"), and in GetBatch fall back to reading any batch when the caller isn't the submitter but holds evidence:inspect (fail closed). Expose submitted-by so the human sees whose batch it is. Test the verb under Cedar and builtin, and the bypass end to end.
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: wrong behaviour or missing companion change.

